        <p class="leading-relaxed text-slate-700 dark:text-slate-300 text-sm sm:text-base mt-4">
          This comparison reveals a distinct divide: ArchColider selected a modular monolith to minimize fixed operational costs during Year 1, whereas Myagis-Forest and Jedis opted for distributed architectures from the start to avoid future structural refactorings. The following sections examine the technical principles underpinning each approach.
        </p>
