      <!-- Section 3 -->
      <section id="dilema-1" class="space-y-6 pt-2">
        <div class="border-b border-slate-200 dark:border-slate-800 pb-3">
          <span class="text-xs font-mono font-bold text-emerald-700 dark:text-emerald-400 uppercase tracking-wider">Section 3</span>
          <h2 class="text-2xl sm:text-3xl font-extrabold text-slate-900 dark:text-slate-100 mt-1">What to Define Before Drawing the First Box?</h2>
        </div>

        <TheoryBox concept="Architecture Characteristics (The Non-Functional Requirements)" chapter="Chapters 3 and 4">
          <p>
            Functional requirements dictate what the system must accomplish. Architecture characteristics (availability, scalability, operational cost, maintainability) govern how the system behaves under real-world production stress.
          </p>
          <p class="mt-2 text-slate-700 dark:text-slate-300">
            In <em>Fundamentals of Software Architecture</em> (Chapter 4), Mark Richards and Neal Ford emphasize that trying to optimize for every possible characteristic simultaneously is an anti-pattern. Every additional characteristic introduces structural complexity, cost, and maintenance friction. A successful system concentrates on a core set of three to five critical characteristics that serve as objective criteria for ruling out alternatives.
          </p>
        </TheoryBox>

        <h3 class="text-xl font-bold text-slate-900 dark:text-slate-100 flex items-center gap-2">
          <span>🥇 ArchColider's Strategy: 4 Guiding Principles to Drive Decisions</span>
        </h3>

        <p class="leading-relaxed text-slate-700 dark:text-slate-300 text-sm sm:text-base">
          Before drawing system components or committing to infrastructure, ArchColider defined four core design principles in their <a href="https://github.com/TheKataLog/ArchColider/blob/master/2.SolutionBackground/SolutionOverview.md#L3-L9" target="_blank" class="text-emerald-700 dark:text-emerald-400 underline font-mono font-semibold">Solution Overview</a> to evaluate every technical trade-off:
        </p>

        <div class="grid grid-cols-1 sm:grid-cols-2 gap-3 text-xs sm:text-sm">
          <div class="p-4 rounded-xl border border-slate-200 dark:border-slate-800 bg-white dark:bg-slate-900 shadow-xs transition-colors">
            <span class="font-bold text-emerald-800 dark:text-emerald-400 font-mono">1. Strive for Cognitive Simplicity</span>
            <p class="text-slate-600 dark:text-slate-400 mt-1 leading-relaxed">The system mental model must remain intuitive for every team member, rejecting layers of indirection or premature abstractions that offer no immediate return.</p>
          </div>
          <div class="p-4 rounded-xl border border-slate-200 dark:border-slate-800 bg-white dark:bg-slate-900 shadow-xs transition-colors">
            <span class="font-bold text-emerald-800 dark:text-emerald-400 font-mono">2. Extensibility and Modifiability in Trade-offs</span>
            <p class="text-slate-600 dark:text-slate-400 mt-1 leading-relaxed">When attributes conflict, favor choices that allow components to be modified, replaced, or extracted as independent services later without global rewrites.</p>
          </div>
          <div class="p-4 rounded-xl border border-slate-200 dark:border-slate-800 bg-white dark:bg-slate-900 shadow-xs transition-colors">
            <span class="font-bold text-emerald-800 dark:text-emerald-400 font-mono">3. Mandatory Telemetry</span>
            <p class="text-slate-600 dark:text-slate-400 mt-1 leading-relaxed">No component enters production without emitting detailed metrics, traces, and logs, ensuring future scaling decisions stem from empirical production data.</p>
          </div>
          <div class="p-4 rounded-xl border border-slate-200 dark:border-slate-800 bg-white dark:bg-slate-900 shadow-xs transition-colors">
            <span class="font-bold text-emerald-800 dark:text-emerald-400 font-mono">4. Messages Over Direct Calls</span>
            <p class="text-slate-600 dark:text-slate-400 mt-1 leading-relaxed">Prioritize asynchronous event messaging to decouple transactional flows from peripheral subsystems, preventing cascading runtime dependencies.</p>
          </div>
        </div>

        <PodiumCounterpoint 
          rank={2} 
          team="Myagis-Forest" 
          title="Myagis-Forest Counterpoint: Explicit Quantitative Targets"
          githubUrl="https://github.com/TheKataLog/Myagis-Forest/blob/main/requirements/architecture-characteristics.md"
          githubLineRange="L1-L25"
          lang="en"
        >
          <p>
            Myagis-Forest complemented qualitative principles by establishing concrete numerical service-level targets up front:
          </p>
          <ul class="list-disc pl-5 space-y-1 mt-2 text-slate-700 dark:text-slate-300 text-xs sm:text-sm">
            <li>Integrating an additional smart fridge manufacturer had to take under 3 engineering days.</li>
            <li>Lunch-hour peak latency: under 1 second for end-user menu browsing queries.</li>
            <li>Support for 100 concurrent active shopping sessions during Year 1 operations.</li>
            <li>Strict isolation of payment card data to qualify for the lightest PCI DSS tier (<ConceptChip id="pci-dss-saq-a" label="SAQ A vs SAQ D" icon="💳" />): by delegating checkout to Stripe through hosted iframes, no cardholder data touches proprietary servers, reducing compliance checks from over 300 technical controls to a brief ~22 question administrative checklist.</li>
          </ul>
        </PodiumCounterpoint>

        <RunnerUpInsight 
          team="da Vinci" 
          tag="Business to Architecture" 
          title="Benefit Dependency Network (BDN): ROI Alignment"
          githubUrl="https://github.com/TheKataLog/da-Vinci/blob/master/solution-discovery/benefit_dependency_network.md#L1-L23"
          githubSnippet="L1-L23"
          lang="en"
        >
          da Vinci built a formal network mapping every architectural choice directly to an objective business return (such as decreasing the onboarding time for new locations). Technical additions lacking measurable operational impact were pruned.
        </RunnerUpInsight>

        <RunnerUpInsight 
          team="Hananoyama" 
          tag="Requirement Validation" 
          title="Critical Audit of Client Operational Assumptions"
          githubUrl="https://github.com/TheKataLog/Hananoyama/blob/main/README.md#L60-L105"
          githubSnippet="L60-L105"
          lang="en"
        >
          Hananoyama began by stress-testing the customer's operational assumptions: they posed critical questions regarding patron behavior and the physical constraints of unattended retail environments.
        </RunnerUpInsight>

        <p class="leading-relaxed text-slate-700 dark:text-slate-300 text-sm sm:text-base mt-4">
          Clarifying architectural quality attributes does not automatically build the system, but it establishes the decision framework: once you understand whether your top priority is time to market, operational cost, or deployment independence, selecting an architectural style becomes an objective exercise.
        </p>
