      <!-- Section 4 -->
      <section id="dilema-2" class="space-y-6 pt-2">
        <div class="border-b border-slate-200 dark:border-slate-800 pb-3">
          <span class="text-xs font-mono font-bold text-emerald-700 dark:text-emerald-400 uppercase tracking-wider">Section 4</span>
          <h2 class="text-2xl sm:text-3xl font-extrabold text-slate-900 dark:text-slate-100 mt-1">The Core Style Decision: Monolith, Microservices, or Serverless?</h2>
        </div>

        <TheoryBox concept="Architectural Quantum and the Fallacies of Distributed Computing" chapter="Chapters 2, 7 and 8">
          <p>
            An <ConceptChip id="architectural-quantum" label="Architectural Quantum" icon="⚛️" /> is the smallest independently deployable unit of a system, featuring high functional cohesion and its own dedicated data store. A monolith consists of a single quantum: if a single background task demands elastic scaling, the entire monolithic artifact must be replicated across servers.
          </p>
          <p class="mt-2">
            <span class="font-semibold text-slate-900 dark:text-slate-100"><ConceptChip id="distributed-fallacies" label="Deutsch's Fallacies" icon="💣" />:</span> Assuming the network is reliable, latency is zero, or bandwidth is infinite. Teams that disregard these realities in early-stage products pay the operational overhead of microservices without realizing their organizational benefits.
          </p>
        </TheoryBox>

        <h3 class="text-xl font-bold text-slate-900 dark:text-slate-100 flex items-center gap-2">
          <span>🥇 ArchColider's Choice: Modular Monolith vs. Microservices</span>
        </h3>

        <p class="leading-relaxed text-slate-700 dark:text-slate-300 text-sm sm:text-base">
          When choosing a baseline architectural style, engineering discussions frequently gravitate toward distributed microservices. In their <a href="https://github.com/TheKataLog/ArchColider/blob/master/4.ADRs/002%20System%20approach.md#L24-L36" target="_blank" class="text-emerald-700 dark:text-emerald-400 underline font-mono font-semibold">ADR 002: System approach</a>, ArchColider constructed a comparative matrix weighing each candidate style against the business's projected transaction scale:
        </p>

        <!-- Help Tip Banner for Matrix Table -->
        <div class="flex items-center gap-2 text-xs text-slate-600 dark:text-slate-400 font-mono my-3 bg-slate-100/80 dark:bg-slate-900/90 px-3.5 py-2.5 rounded-xl border border-slate-200 dark:border-slate-800 transition-colors">
