      <!-- Section 5 -->
      <section id="dilema-3" class="space-y-6 pt-2">
        <div class="border-b border-slate-200 dark:border-slate-800 pb-3">
          <span class="text-xs font-mono font-bold text-emerald-700 dark:text-emerald-400 uppercase tracking-wider">Section 5</span>
          <h2 class="text-2xl sm:text-3xl font-extrabold text-slate-900 dark:text-slate-100 mt-1">How to Decompose the Domain? (Bounded Contexts)</h2>
        </div>

        <TheoryBox concept="Domain Partitioning vs. Technical Layer Partitioning" chapter="Chapters 8 and 9">
          <p>
            Technical partitioning organizes code by horizontal technological layers (controllers, services, repositories): any change to a business requirement forces edits across all layers. Domain partitioning organizes code around business capabilities (Orders, Inventory, Billing), encapsulating business rules so modifications stay confined to their respective context.
          </p>
        </TheoryBox>

        <h3 class="text-xl font-bold text-slate-900 dark:text-slate-100 flex items-center gap-2">
          <span>🥇 ArchColider's DDD Strategy: Strategic Subdomain Categorization</span>
        </h3>

        <p class="leading-relaxed text-slate-700 dark:text-slate-300 text-sm sm:text-base">
          Rather than organizing code into technical layers, ArchColider applied Domain-Driven Design (DDD) to partition their modules into <ConceptChip id="bounded-contexts" label="Bounded Contexts" icon="🗺️" />. To maximize development return for their small team, they categorized subdomains into three tiers of <ConceptChip id="strategic-subdomains" label="Strategic Subdomains" icon="🎯" /> (<a href="https://github.com/TheKataLog/ArchColider/blob/master/2.SolutionBackground/SolutionOverview.md#L27-L47" target="_blank" class="text-emerald-700 dark:text-emerald-400 underline font-mono font-semibold">see SolutionOverview.md</a>):
        </p>

        <div class="grid grid-cols-1 sm:grid-cols-3 gap-3 text-xs">
          <div class="p-4 sm:p-5 rounded-xl border border-slate-200 dark:border-slate-800 bg-white dark:bg-slate-900 shadow-xs flex flex-col transition-colors">
            <span class="inline-flex items-center gap-1.5 px-2.5 py-0.5 rounded text-xs font-mono font-bold bg-emerald-100 dark:bg-emerald-950/70 text-emerald-800 dark:text-emerald-300 border border-emerald-300 dark:border-emerald-700/60 w-fit mb-2">Core Domain</span>
            <div class="text-xs text-slate-600 dark:text-slate-400 mb-3 font-medium leading-relaxed">Bespoke custom software providing direct competitive advantage.</div>
            <ul class="text-slate-700 dark:text-slate-300 space-y-1.5 list-disc pl-4 text-xs mt-auto">
              <li><span class="font-semibold text-slate-900 dark:text-slate-100">Meal Catalog:</span> Nutritional data, allergens, and real-time stock per fridge.</li>
              <li><span class="font-semibold text-slate-900 dark:text-slate-100">Order Processing:</span> Core engine managing transactions and subscriptions.</li>
              <li><span class="font-semibold text-slate-900 dark:text-slate-100">Loyalty & Rewards:</span> Proprietary retention mechanics and reward tiering.</li>
            </ul>
          </div>
          <div class="p-4 sm:p-5 rounded-xl border border-slate-200 dark:border-slate-800 bg-white dark:bg-slate-900 shadow-xs flex flex-col transition-colors">
            <span class="inline-flex items-center gap-1.5 px-2.5 py-0.5 rounded text-xs font-mono font-bold bg-slate-100 dark:bg-slate-800 text-slate-800 dark:text-slate-200 border border-slate-300 dark:border-slate-700/80 w-fit mb-2">Supporting Domain</span>
            <div class="text-xs text-slate-600 dark:text-slate-400 mb-3 font-medium leading-relaxed">Necessary operational functionality without proprietary competitive edge.</div>
            <ul class="text-slate-700 dark:text-slate-300 space-y-1.5 list-disc pl-4 text-xs mt-auto">
              <li><span class="font-semibold text-slate-900 dark:text-slate-100">Feedback & Surveys:</span> Asynchronous post-purchase customer surveys.</li>
              <li><span class="font-semibold text-slate-900 dark:text-slate-100">Kitchen Scheduling:</span> Order batching dispatched to ghost kitchen facilities.</li>
            </ul>
          </div>
          <div class="p-4 sm:p-5 rounded-xl border border-slate-200 dark:border-slate-800 bg-white dark:bg-slate-900 shadow-xs flex flex-col transition-colors">
            <span class="inline-flex items-center gap-1.5 px-2.5 py-0.5 rounded text-xs font-mono font-bold bg-slate-100 dark:bg-slate-800 text-slate-800 dark:text-slate-200 border border-slate-300 dark:border-slate-700/80 w-fit mb-2">Generic Domain</span>
            <div class="text-xs text-slate-600 dark:text-slate-400 mb-3 font-medium leading-relaxed">Commodity capabilities best handled by commercial SaaS or OSS libraries.</div>
            <ul class="text-slate-700 dark:text-slate-300 space-y-1.5 list-disc pl-4 text-xs mt-auto">
              <li><span class="font-semibold text-slate-900 dark:text-slate-100">Payments:</span> Delegated to Stripe (zero cardholder data stored internally).</li>
              <li><span class="font-semibold text-slate-900 dark:text-slate-100">Notifications:</span> Twilio for SMS and SendGrid for automated emails.</li>
              <li><span class="font-semibold text-slate-900 dark:text-slate-100">Reporting:</span> Dashboards built with off-the-shelf business intelligence tools.</li>
            </ul>
          </div>
        </div>

        <PodiumCounterpoint 
          rank={2} 
          team="Myagis-Forest" 
          title="Myagis-Forest: Context Map Focused on Perishable Logistics"
          githubUrl="https://github.com/TheKataLog/Myagis-Forest/blob/main/architecture/ddd-context-map.md"
          lang="en"
        >
          <p>
            Myagis-Forest designed a formal DDD Context Map centered on the shelf-life management of fresh food items. Because inventory spoils rapidly, stock inaccuracies result in immediate financial losses. They designated the real-time synchronization between smart fridge inventory and ghost kitchen prep schedules as their primary Core Domain.
          </p>
