        <!-- 9.1: Constraints and Principles -->
        <div class="p-4 rounded-xl bg-slate-50 dark:bg-slate-800/40 border border-slate-200 dark:border-slate-800 space-y-2">
            <div class="font-bold text-xs font-mono uppercase text-emerald-800 dark:text-emerald-300 flex items-center gap-1.5">
              <span>🌐</span>
              <span>Perimeter Defense: Layer 7 Auth Offloading (Security.md)</span>
            </div>
            <p class="text-xs sm:text-sm text-slate-700 dark:text-slate-300 leading-relaxed">
              To conserve EC2 CPU cycles from parsing and verifying JWT signatures on every inbound request, authentication was offloaded to the network edge via <ConceptChip id="layer7-auth-offloading" label="Load Balancer Auth Offloading (ALB + Cognito)" icon="🌐" />: the Layer 7 ALB validates tokens against Cognito and only forwards authenticated traffic with signed headers to private EC2 instances.
            </p>
          </div>
          <div class="space-y-4">
          <h3 class="text-lg sm:text-xl font-bold text-slate-900 dark:text-slate-100 flex items-center gap-2">
            <span>9.1 Global Constraints and 4 Core Design Principles</span>
          </h3>
          <p class="leading-relaxed text-slate-700 dark:text-slate-300 text-sm sm:text-base">
            In their <a href="https://github.com/TheKataLog/ArchColider/blob/master/1.ProblemBackground/Constraints.md" target="_blank" class="text-emerald-700 dark:text-emerald-400 underline font-mono font-semibold">Constraints.md</a> document, ArchColider identified four governing constraints:
          </p>

          <div class="grid grid-cols-1 sm:grid-cols-2 gap-3 text-xs sm:text-sm">
            <div class="p-3.5 rounded-lg border border-slate-200 dark:border-slate-800 bg-slate-50/70 dark:bg-slate-950/60">
              <span class="font-bold text-slate-900 dark:text-slate-100 font-mono">1. Small Engineering Team</span>
              <p class="text-slate-600 dark:text-slate-400 mt-1 leading-relaxed"><em>"Development team is limited, so the solution should be simple at the beginning to prove business ideas."</em> Avoid squandering engineering bandwidth on complex distributed scaffolding.</p>
            </div>
            <div class="p-3.5 rounded-lg border border-slate-200 dark:border-slate-800 bg-slate-50/70 dark:bg-slate-950/60">
              <span class="font-bold text-slate-900 dark:text-slate-100 font-mono">2. Fast Time-to-Market</span>
              <p class="text-slate-600 dark:text-slate-400 mt-1 leading-relaxed"><em>"Time-to-market is critical, and with support of the previous constraint, it should be super simple to deploy."</em> Clean, frictionless release pipelines.</p>
            </div>
            <div class="p-3.5 rounded-lg border border-slate-200 dark:border-slate-800 bg-slate-50/70 dark:bg-slate-950/60">
              <span class="font-bold text-slate-900 dark:text-slate-100 font-mono">3. AWS Primary Target</span>
              <p class="text-slate-600 dark:text-slate-400 mt-1 leading-relaxed"><em>"AWS is the primary target platform for deployment."</em> Rely on managed cloud primitives in us-east close to Detroit.</p>
            </div>
            <div class="p-3.5 rounded-lg border border-slate-200 dark:border-slate-800 bg-slate-50/70 dark:bg-slate-950/60">
              <span class="font-bold text-slate-900 dark:text-slate-100 font-mono">4. Tight Budget</span>
              <p class="text-slate-600 dark:text-slate-400 mt-1 leading-relaxed"><em>"Budget is very limited, so OSS and tools provided by the target platform should end up higher in prioritization."</em> Prioritize open source and economical SaaS solutions.</p>
            </div>
          </div>

          <p class="leading-relaxed text-slate-700 dark:text-slate-300 text-sm sm:text-base mt-3">
            From these constraints, the team formalized four guiding design principles in their <a href="https://github.com/TheKataLog/ArchColider/blob/master/2.SolutionBackground/SolutionOverview.md" target="_blank" class="text-emerald-700 dark:text-emerald-400 underline font-mono font-semibold">Solution Overview</a>:
          </p>

          <div class="grid grid-cols-1 sm:grid-cols-2 gap-3 text-xs sm:text-sm">
            <div class="p-4 rounded-xl border border-emerald-200 dark:border-emerald-800/60 bg-emerald-50/40 dark:bg-emerald-950/20">
              <div class="font-mono font-bold text-emerald-900 dark:text-emerald-300 flex items-center gap-1.5 mb-1">
                <span>Principle 1</span>
                <span class="text-slate-500 font-normal">· Simplicity</span>
              </div>
              <span class="block font-bold text-slate-900 dark:text-slate-100">Strive for cognitive simplicity</span>
              <p class="text-slate-600 dark:text-slate-400 mt-1 leading-relaxed">The architecture must remain straightforward to reason about and operate. Reject abstractions that introduce conceptual overhead without measurable value.</p>
            </div>

            <div class="p-4 rounded-xl border border-emerald-200 dark:border-emerald-800/60 bg-emerald-50/40 dark:bg-emerald-950/20">
              <div class="font-mono font-bold text-emerald-900 dark:text-emerald-300 flex items-center gap-1.5 mb-1">
                <span>Principle 2</span>
                <span class="text-slate-500 font-normal">· Evolution</span>
              </div>
              <span class="block font-bold text-slate-900 dark:text-slate-100">Extensibility and modifiability preferred in trade-offs</span>
              <p class="text-slate-600 dark:text-slate-400 mt-1 leading-relaxed">When system attributes conflict, favor designs that allow extracting standalone services in the future without painful code rewrites.</p>
            </div>

            <div class="p-4 rounded-xl border border-emerald-200 dark:border-emerald-800/60 bg-emerald-50/40 dark:bg-emerald-950/20">
              <div class="font-mono font-bold text-emerald-900 dark:text-emerald-300 flex items-center gap-1.5 mb-1">
                <span>Principle 3</span>
                <span class="text-slate-500 font-normal">· Observability</span>
              </div>
              <span class="block font-bold text-slate-900 dark:text-slate-100">Telemetry is mandatory</span>
              <p class="text-slate-600 dark:text-slate-400 mt-1 leading-relaxed">Every subdomain must emit metrics and traces. Future decisions to decompose modules into services must rely on hard performance data.</p>
            </div>

            <div class="p-4 rounded-xl border border-emerald-200 dark:border-emerald-800/60 bg-emerald-50/40 dark:bg-emerald-950/20">
              <div class="font-mono font-bold text-emerald-900 dark:text-emerald-300 flex items-center gap-1.5 mb-1">
                <span>Principle 4</span>
                <span class="text-slate-500 font-normal">· Decoupling</span>
              </div>
              <span class="block font-bold text-slate-900 dark:text-slate-100">Messages over direct calls</span>
              <p class="text-slate-600 dark:text-slate-400 mt-1 leading-relaxed">Favor asynchronous events to isolate core transactions from peripheral consumers, avoiding cascading failure modes.</p>
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>

